%I A398669 #11 Aug 17 2026 16:25:40
%S A398669 1,1,2,4,10,29,95,320,1162,4406,17825,76704,352058,1704355
%N A398669 Number of equivalence classes of length n words over an infinite alphabet such that all prefixes satisfy c(i) >= c(j) if f(i) < f(j) where c(i) is the number of occurrences of the letter i, f(i) = floor(sqrt(2*i) + 1/2), and words are equivalent under relabeling of letters with equal values of f(i).
%C A398669 The relations of the letters form a partial order of the natural numbers shown below:
%C A398669   ...
%C A398669  4 5 6
%C A398669   3 2
%C A398669    1
%H A398669 John Tyler Rascoe, <a href="/A398669/a398669_1.py.txt">Python code</a>.
%e A398669 The word of length 5 (1,2,1,3,4) is equivalent to (1,2,1,3,5), (1,2,1,3,6), (1,3,1,2,4), (1,3,1,2,5), and (1,3,1,2,6) so this is one equivalence class counted under a(5) = 29.
%e A398669 a(1) = 1: (1).
%e A398669 a(2) = 2: (1,1), (1,2).
%e A398669 a(3) = 4: (1,1,1), (1,1,2), (1,2,1), (1,2,3).
